#, python-format
msgid ""
"Your battery ended this period %(residual)s less charged than it started,"
" so part of the grid import it avoided was paid for out of the charge it "
"began with rather than earned by its dispatch. The benchmark is not "
"allowed to do that — it must finish at the state of charge it started "
"from — so the two are only comparable once that residual is accounted "
"for. On that basis your policy captures %(pct)s percent of the grid "
"import a perfectly-informed battery could have avoided. Perfect foresight"
" knows every future price exactly and no real controller reaches it, so "
"treat this as a floor on what a better policy could achieve, not as a "
"target."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your battery is wired across the phases in a way version 1 does not "
"model, so this run uses the 3-phase approximation you accepted. Because a"
" smart meter nets across phases the energy result should be close; what "
"is not modelled is the per-phase power limit, which a 1-phase battery "
"cannot exceed however the load is distributed."
msgstr ""

